              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ধোপা (dhopā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from dhauvati, \"washes\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 6886). CDIAL lists dhopā, \"washerman\", among the later forms built on it."
            }
